            {"h": "The one-higher-or-lower rule", "ul": ["You can play a card from the peaks if it is exactly one rank higher or one rank lower than the card on top of the waste pile. A 6 goes on a 5 or a 7. Suits do not matter.", "Ace and King count as neighbours, so you can go from a King to an Ace and the other way round.", "A card is only playable when no other card is covering it. At the start only the bottom row is free; each time you remove cards, more of the row above is uncovered.", "The card you play becomes the new top of the waste, and the next play is measured against it."]},
